<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<configuration>

  <!-- Scoped to Goop.PackageTests only. Every other project in the repo keeps
       the machine-wide NuGet configuration untouched.

       This file adds NOTHING today: the <packageSources> element below is empty
       apart from the commented-out entry, and because there is no <clear />,
       the inherited sources (nuget.org and anything machine-wide) still apply.
       That is what lets the placeholder test restore its MSTest packages before
       milestone M8 exists.

       TODO (M8): uncomment the local feed once `dotnet pack` is producing a
       .nupkg, then add <PackageReference Include="Goop" Version="0.1.0" /> to
       the csproj. A "folder feed" is literally a directory of .nupkg files -
       NuGet treats it as a source with no server involved.

       NOTE ON THE PATH: relative paths here resolve against the directory
       containing THIS file (dotnet/tests/Goop.PackageTests/), so the value
       below points at dotnet/artifacts/packages. If `dotnet pack` is instead
       configured to output to the REPO-ROOT artifacts/ folder - which is what
       .gitignore is set up for - this needs one more level:
       ..\..\..\artifacts\packages. Settle that when M8 is wired up and make the
       pack output path and this source agree.

       Also consider adding <clear /> at that point, so a restore cannot
       accidentally be satisfied by a real package from nuget.org that happens to
       be called Goop. -->

  <packageSources>
    <!-- <add key="goop-local" value="..\..\artifacts\packages" /> -->
  </packageSources>

</configuration>
